CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#94: FILE: arch/x86/include/asm/amd_nb.h:16:
+extern void k8_fake_nodes(const struct bootnode *nodes, int nr_nodes);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

WARNING:MISPLACED_INIT: __initdata should be placed after nodeids[8]
#106: FILE: arch/x86/mm/k8topology_64.c:30:
+static unsigned char __initdata nodeids[8];

It is possible to use section markers on variables in a way
which gcc doesn't understand (or at least not the way the
developer intended)::

  static struct __initdata samsung_pll_clock exynos4_plls[nr_plls] = {

does not put exynos4_plls in the .initdata section. The __initdata
marker can be virtually anywhere on the line, except right after
"struct". The preferred location is before the "=" sign if there is
one, or before the trailing ";" otherwise.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/1377655732.3619.19.camel@joe-AO722/

CHECK:MULTIPLE_ASSIGNMENTS: multiple assignments should be avoided
#137: FILE: arch/x86/mm/k8topology_64.c:105:
+		nodeids[i] = nodeid = limit & 7;

Multiple assignments on a single line makes the code unnecessarily
complicated. So on a single line assign value to a single variable
only, this makes the code more readable and helps avoid typos.

